{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562319-judges-and-the-arisen","id":562319,"title":"Judges and the Arisen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-20T16:23:54-07:00","id":562319,"title":"Judges and the Arisen","content":"I'm fuzzy on the relationship between a mummy and her Judge. Is she the one being judged, or does she seek out those who deserve judgement? Have I simply overlooked the part of the core book that talks about this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T16:30:08-07:00","id":562334,"title":"","content":"The book isn't as explicit as it could be, but I believe it's pretty clear that the Arisen seeks out those who deserve Judgement. When an Arisen experienced the Rite of Return, she descended into Duat and stood before the Judges. Each of the 42 tested her, shredding her soul with every encounter. The Final Judge touched the core of her being, her Defining Pillar, and deemed her worthy of being its servant for all time.<br /> <br /> So, in other words, the Arisen has already been judged. One of the ways of earning a Descent reset is to do something your Judge approves of, and generally speaking exacting a harsh judgement on someone who has committed a sin against your specific Judge seems like a fine way to earn that reset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T17:25:28-07:00","id":562381,"title":"","content":"The Mummies are the servants of the 42 Judges. Mind you, its left deliberately vague who's the actual Judge they're following - could be old gods, could be the ascended Shan'itu (spelling?). But the Mummies are definitely the servant-slaves who are tasked with world domination through recreating Irem.<br /> <br /> In a way, Mummy is a game where you're playing a zombie raised by a necromancer and sent to do their bidding, like any other fantasy necromancer-zombie relationship save for the fact the necromancer is a godling. There's the temptation to play the necromancer-god on a smaller scale yourself with the cult, and the potential to become free again through Apothesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T00:46:32-07:00","id":563795,"title":"","content":"I think Mummies are mostly a little fuzzy on the relationship, too, as they tend to be about most things. They know what specific Judge they serve, and that Judge's general characteristics, but other than that all they necessarily know is that they have standing orders to retrieve Relics and that it's a bad idea to talk smack about Irem. The different Guilds seem to have more or less set goals for themselves, based on their memories of Irem. It's debatable how much the Judges or the Shan'iatu (wherever and whatever they may now be) really care about re-creating Irem in the world of the living, but it is something that a lot of Mummies see as a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T01:06:35-07:00","id":563803,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that the Arisen serve a Judge whose crime/sin they're guilty of, but that's just one interpretation and I would never try to say that it's canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T17:42:55-07:00","id":565892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562319-judges-and-the-arisen?p=563803#post563803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that the Arisen serve a Judge whose crime/sin they're guilty of, but that's just one interpretation and I would never try to say that it's canon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that's a good way to go with it. After all, there's got to be <i>some </i>reason why a particular Judge chooses a particular Mummy; they don't seem like the kind of beings that act randomly or on a whim. Perhaps when the other judges accuse a Mummy of a crime of which he is guilty, it tears at the Mummy's soul because he feels remorse at what he's done and accepts his punishment. When he meets his final judge, however, he stands accused of a crime which he doesn't believe he has committed, or which he refuses to repent, and he instead makes his decree in an effort to justify himself.<br /> <br /> For instance, a Mummy passes before 41 judges, before at last finding herself standing before Akhi, the Roar. It accuses her of giving voice, during a fit of rage, to blasphemous curses against one of the Shan'iatu who had overseen her guild. Though exhausted by her ordeals, she hardens her heart, telling the Judge that her passion was what defined her and gave her strength, and that she will not apologize for it. Akhi offers an enigmatic nod of his terrible head, and before she can figure out if he approves or disapproves of her defense, she is jarred into wakefulness by her first Descent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T17:50:29-07:00","id":565895,"title":"","content":"Hm. I'm less comfortable with that as a jumping off point. All Arisen beginning their existence with an act of defiance runs contrary to, well, just about everything we know about the Rite and the Judges. I wouldn't assume guilt or innocence in regards to a particular Judge's purview. The Arisen are, ultimately, tools, so it seems more likely to me that each Judge would claim an Arisen best suited to persecuting those who are guilty of the Judge's chosen crimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T18:32:08-07:00","id":565916,"title":"","content":"One thing; the 42 Assessors of Maat asked you if you were guilty of their crimes, and your job was to protest each and every accusation. If Irem is similar to later Egypt, then perhaps your chosen Judge is the one you couldn't deny your guilt to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T19:27:30-07:00","id":565973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562319-judges-and-the-arisen?p=565895#post565895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I'm less comfortable with that as a jumping off point. All Arisen beginning their existence with an act of defiance runs contrary to, well, just about everything we know about the Rite and the Judges. I wouldn't assume guilt or innocence in regards to a particular Judge's purview. The Arisen are, ultimately, tools, so it seems more likely to me that each Judge would claim an Arisen best suited to persecuting those who are guilty of the Judge's chosen crimes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, but think of it this way: the Judges probed, prodded, and dissected the Arisen *until* they dared to commit an act of defiance. In doing so they laid bare the hidden unworthiness of the Mummy's soul... and perhaps that's where the true punishment began.<br /> <br /> The Arisen can <i>never</i> remember what happens to them in Duat between descents; for all we know, henet is an endless parade of torments and brutal rites of purification at the hands of their Judge. They can escape this punishment only temporarily, and even then only to do the will of the Judges on earth. Should they neglect their duties, they fall back into hell all the quicker.<br /> <br /> Perhaps those who would become Arisen were chosen by the Shan'iatu specifically because they seemed likely to offer defiance to the Judges. Perhaps the Rite of Return <i>required</i> that the Judges find the Mummy-to-be unworthy, so that they would be denied a the bliss of the afterlife. The Shan'iatu had already bribed Ammut to participate in their plan, so instead of being devoured, the Arisen entered a limbo state of perpetual punishment and service.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-23-2015, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T20:09:57-07:00","id":565988,"title":"","content":"I look at how the Deceived speculate on the best means to lay &quot;siege&quot; to Duat and can't help but feel that rebellious servants would be the last thing a Judge would want for their Arisen, in practical terms. More generally, however, I don't like the idea of mandating that all Arisen characters must have faced their Judge and rejected their judgement. It's a bit limiting, concept-wise. I'm not sure it even makes sense for all the Decrees. Ab and Ka I can see an argument with, for sure, but the others seem like they would vary greatly. To rationalise their existence would mean allowing only a limited interpretation of each Decree's character, something I don't see as beneficial.<br /> <br /> I suppose I just see it as limiting the setting/available character options, rather than embellishing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T22:53:34-07:00","id":566138,"title":"","content":"All good points, and furthermore it's probably best to leave the nature of Duat undefined, for the most point. It's fun to speculate, though. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T03:10:08-07:00","id":566215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I look at how the Deceived speculate on the best means to lay &quot;siege&quot; to Duat and can't help but feel that rebellious servants would be the last thing a Judge would want for their Arisen, </div> </div> </div>To me the obvious reason would that the Arisen need a degree of defiance and spiritual strength in them to become what they are. A totally loyal empty shell for the will of the Shaniatu just wouldn't have worked. Plus the entire memory lose/descent could indicate that the Arisen need to be heavily controlled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T03:58:51-07:00","id":566233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562319-judges-and-the-arisen?p=566215#post566215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me the obvious reason would that the Arisen need a degree of defiance and spiritual strength in them to become what they are. A totally loyal empty shell for the will of the Shaniatu just wouldn't have worked. Plus the entire memory lose/descent could indicate that the Arisen need to be heavily controlled.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say there's a difference between strength of character and defiance towards their culture's gods, specifically.<br /> <br /> It has actually been mentioned that Arisen all have a strength of character, that the attributes that would make a perfect slave would not be found in people with the fortitude to endure the Rite. But that's not quite the same as saying &quot;All Arisen were chosen because they defied their Judge&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T05:01:03-07:00","id":566264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562319-judges-and-the-arisen?p=566138#post566138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All good points, and furthermore it's probably best to leave the nature of Duat undefined, for the most point. It's fun to speculate, though. :P</div> </div> </div> </div> Personal Cosmology Warning - what I say below has to do my head cannon, nothing official.<br /> <br /> While I don't quite define Duat, I do define the Judges as the Old Gods, similar to the ones kicked out of the Supernal by the Exarchs. As of 1e, the Supernal was a critical part of the flow of souls between the material world, and the spiritual. When someone was born, their soul came from these heavenly realms, lived in the flesh, died, and then their soul traveled back to the Supernal. Duat, as the land where souls traveled to, was something related to this cycle. As well, the Supernal is big on the whole True Name thing, which is a fairly big theme in Mummy as well, with how Utterances work, and all. Destiny is also tied into the Supernal, different from the Wyrd and God Machine's version of Fate.<br /> <br /> So, the sorcerer-kings and Judges are the Old Gods. When the Shan'iatu tried to become Judges, they ended up becoming corrupted things, as if tainted by the Lower Depths or Abyss. Thus, the failing of their powers over time as it was sucked out, until they effectively became twisted demon lords known as the Judges of Death, who are hungry for control of the world.<br /> <br /> This ties into the theme of Mummy - power is slavery, as their lords and master are effectively slavish archdevils.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562319-judges-and-the-arisen?p=565895#post565895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I'm less comfortable with that as a jumping off point. All Arisen beginning their existence with an act of defiance runs contrary to, well, just about everything we know about the Rite and the Judges. I wouldn't assume guilt or innocence in regards to a particular Judge's purview. The Arisen are, ultimately, tools, so it seems more likely to me that each Judge would claim an Arisen best suited to persecuting those who are guilty of the Judge's chosen crimes.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wouldn't call it an act of defiance. Changelings escaping from the Gentry to make their way back to Earth is an act of defiance. What the Arisen go through to become a mummy is more of a trial or test -- its an attempt to see if they have a core sense of self that can withstand the test of time. Those that succeed are then sent back.<br /> <br /> One of the central conflicts of Mummy is around losing your sense of self with the loss of your Memory. I feel that the original Rite of Return is tied into that conflict, that its a statement about Memory and Self, not defiance or power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-24-2015, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T05:12:18-07:00","id":566266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562319-judges-and-the-arisen?p=566264#post566264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't call it an act of defiance. Changelings escaping from the Gentry to make their way back to Earth is an act of defiance. What the Arisen go through to become a mummy is more of a trial or test -- its an attempt to see if they have a core sense of self that can withstand the test of time. Those that succeed are then sent back.</div> </div> </div> </div>As written in the core? Yes, absolutely. But I was responding to a post that literally used the word &quot;defiance&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T05:16:04-07:00","id":566273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562319-judges-and-the-arisen?p=566266#post566266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As written in the core? Yes, absolutely. But I was responding to a post that literally used the word &quot;defiance&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wasn't disagreeing with you, just putting my own thoughts on the matter down.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T11:17:15-07:00","id":566709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562319-judges-and-the-arisen?p=566264#post566264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the sorcerer-kings and Judges are the Old Gods. When the Shan'iatu tried to become Judges, they ended up becoming corrupted things, as if tainted by the Lower Depths or Abyss. Thus, the failing of their powers over time as it was sucked out, until they effectively became twisted demon lords known as the Judges of Death, who are hungry for control of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe the Shan'iatu were particularly interested in being judges, or in obtaining any sort of Godlike power (for much of their existence they already had that). What they really wanted was access to the Aaru. They say as much in Decieved. This is essentially the guiding star of Shan'iatu existence. Everything they do... every corruption they endure... seems to be on the alter of this quest. Besides, the Shan'iatu made 42 judges somehow, but only 35 Shan'iatu vanished.<br /> <br /> Now, certainly the Shan'iatu made new Judges with Necromancy, because the Old Judges... being loyal emanations of Ma'at... wouldn't allow them Aaru. Just, I don't believe those Judges were them, or ever intended to be.<br /> <br /> They pulled the same Azar trick they do in the book. 'We will make a a new God'. It's something they do over and over again... since the people in charge of them are disliked, they just engineer new ones!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T12:58:44-07:00","id":566825,"title":"","content":"Well, this and that are separate issues. Like I said, personal cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T16:55:38-07:00","id":567129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562319-judges-and-the-arisen?p=566709#post566709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't believe the Shan'iatu were particularly interested in being judges, or in obtaining any sort of Godlike power (for much of their existence they already had that). What they really wanted was access to the Aaru. They say as much in Decieved. This is essentially the guiding star of Shan'iatu existence. Everything they do... every corruption they endure... seems to be on the alter of this quest. Besides, the Shan'iatu made 42 judges somehow, but only 35 Shan'iatu vanished.<br /> <br /> Now, certainly the Shan'iatu made new Judges with Necromancy, because the Old Judges... being loyal emanations of Ma'at... wouldn't allow them Aaru. Just, I don't believe those Judges were them, or ever intended to be.<br /> <br /> They pulled the same Azar trick they do in the book. 'We will make a a new God'. It's something they do over and over again... since the people in charge of them are disliked, they just engineer new ones!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, if we can completely believe the reported memories of one Deceived Temakh (which we absolutely cannot), the Shan'iatu were definitely interested in cosmic power of some sort, and were specifically trying to become &quot;lords of death&quot; and &quot;claim the seal of Law.&quot;<br /> <br /> In any event, the Deceived account seems to cast Ammut as the architect of the Rite of Return, and everything connected with it. Anpu warns that the Rite is a &quot;tendril of the Devourer&quot; which, with the aid of the Shan'iatu will &quot;become a hand smothering the world.&quot; I wouldn't be surprised if the Shan'iatu who weren't betrayed are now entirely at her mercy.<br /> <br /> Another troubling thought is that, since the Arisen can't really be destroyed, but <i>can</i> become corrupted into Shaunkhsen, in the fullness of time it becomes an inevitability that all remaining, active Mummies will be either Shaunkhsen or Deceived. Presumably this was part of Ammut's plan when she gave the Rite of Return to the Shan'iatu, though it seems likely that the creation of the Deceived was not something she anticipated. This could conceivably make the Deceived the universe's only hope in some distant future period... which is not an encouraging thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T17:10:14-07:00","id":567133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562319-judges-and-the-arisen?p=566273#post566273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I wasn't disagreeing with you, just putting my own thoughts on the matter down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, ok. Just a tad confusing, since you were quoting me and coming at the discussion from a different framework. No harm done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562319-judges-and-the-arisen?p=567129#post567129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another troubling thought is that, since the Arisen can't really be destroyed, but <i>can</i> become corrupted into Shaunkhsen, in the fullness of time it becomes an inevitability that all remaining, active Mummies will be either Shaunkhsen or Deceived. Presumably this was part of Ammut's plan when she gave the Rite of Return to the Shan'iatu, though it seems likely that the creation of the Deceived was not something she anticipated. This could conceivably make the Deceived the universe's only hope in some distant future period... which is not an encouraging thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would guess that this is absolutely Ammut's plan. She isn't so much patient as she is inevitable, befitting the forces she embodies.<br /> <br /> People have posited a situation before in which, in some distant future, the only remnants of humanity are a horde of slavery Shuankhsen preparing for a confrontation against a handful of ascended Deceived. Just as the Arisen have nowhere to go but down, the Deceived have nowhere to go but up. Fate's servants against Ammut's, with the final fate of the universe at stake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T18:32:28-07:00","id":567214,"title":"","content":"When I initially was reading this I was going to post that End of Days <b>Mummy</b> scenario because, unless I'm unaware of other posters, that's what I came up with on this board once <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:28:14-07:00","id":567996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562319-judges-and-the-arisen?p=567129#post567129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another troubling thought is that, since the Arisen can't really be destroyed, but <i>can</i> become corrupted into Shaunkhsen, in the fullness of time it becomes an inevitability that all remaining, active Mummies will be either Shaunkhsen or Deceived. Presumably this was part of Ammut's plan when she gave the Rite of Return to the Shan'iatu, though it seems likely that the creation of the Deceived was not something she anticipated. This could conceivably make the Deceived the universe's only hope in some distant future period... which is not an encouraging thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they all get Seattle`d.<br /> And what an awful book that is for mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T14:19:46-07:00","id":569574,"title":"","content":"It would be kind of hilarious if Ammut's millennia-spanning plans were foiled by some kind of cosmic computer glitch in Seattle.<br /> <br /> &quot;Curse you Seattle! Cuuuuurse you!!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T07:57:53-07:00","id":572638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/562319-judges-and-the-arisen?p=565916#post565916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing; the 42 Assessors of Maat asked you if you were guilty of their crimes, and your job was to protest each and every accusation. If Irem is similar to later Egypt, then perhaps your chosen Judge is the one you couldn't deny your guilt to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they quizzed you about the crimes of the Shan'iatu - and the Shan'iatu would be guilt of a <i>lot</i> of the crimes the Judges preside over - and chose as their servants those who sold out their former masters for the sake of the Eternal Law those masters were trying to defy. That would turn the Rite into a battle that the Shan'iatu lost - their attempt to create new Judges was coopted by the old ones who used it to take over stewardship of the Arisen - and Ammut laughed as the Judges consigned the Shan'iatu to her maw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}